<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shibl al-Dawla Nasr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1038</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shibl al-Dawla Nasr was the Mirdasid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> from 1029 to 1038, son of the dynasty's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salih-ibn-mirdas">Salih ibn Mirdas</a>. In 1030 he defeated the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iii-argyros">Romanos III</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azaz">Azaz</a>, but then accepted Byzantine protection to secure his rule. He was killed in 1038 fighting a Fatimid army, and Aleppo briefly passed to Fatimid control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shibl-al-dawla-nasr.jpg" alt="Shibl al-Dawla Nasr" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not credited · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silver_dirham_of_Nasr_ibn_Salih.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
